WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.355
Security tools process enormous amounts of data and generate valuable alerts,

00:00:04.355 --> 00:00:07.063
but no detection system has complete coverage.

00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:10.544
Rules reflect known conditions, available telemetry, configuration choices, thresholds,

00:00:10.544 --> 00:00:13.252
and assumptions about how threats will appear.

00:00:13.252 --> 00:00:17.506
Some activity may remain below an alert threshold, resemble legitimate work,

00:00:17.506 --> 00:00:19.827
occur in a poorly monitored environment,

00:00:19.827 --> 00:00:23.695
or use a pattern that existing analytics do not recognize.

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:28.337
A missing alert therefore does not always mean an absence of risk.

00:00:28.337 --> 00:00:31.432
Threat hunting helps organizations investigate those uncertain areas.

00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:35.300
Analysts can ask whether an important scenario would be visible,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.847
whether expected evidence exists,

00:00:36.847 --> 00:00:41.489
and whether activity in the environment is consistent with normal business operations.

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:45.744
This proactive work can reduce risk by finding suspicious activity earlier.

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:49.612
Earlier understanding gives security teams more time to validate evidence,

00:00:49.612 --> 00:00:51.546
protect affected services, coordinate stakeholders,

00:00:51.546 --> 00:00:54.253
and decide whether incident-response procedures are necessary.

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.187
Hunting also evaluates defensive assumptions.

00:00:56.187 --> 00:01:00.829
A team may believe that a data source is complete or that

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:03.150
a detection covers a particular behavior.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:07.018
A hunt can reveal missing systems, inconsistent logging, noisy analytics,

00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:09.726
or conditions that the detection never considered.

00:01:09.726 --> 00:01:14.754
Organizations can use hunts to focus attention on high-value assets and business processes.

00:01:14.754 --> 00:01:17.462
Identity services, critical applications, sensitive data environments,

00:01:17.462 --> 00:01:23.264
and externally accessible services often deserve deeper visibility because their compromise could create greater impact.

00:01:23.264 --> 00:01:28.293
The value of hunting is broader than the number of confirmed threats found.

00:01:28.293 --> 00:01:31.387
Improvements to telemetry, asset ownership, analytical methods, detections,

00:01:31.387 --> 00:01:34.482
and cross-team communication all strengthen the security program.

00:01:34.482 --> 00:01:39.123
Threat hunting does not eliminate cyber risk, replace monitoring, or guarantee discovery.

00:01:39.123 --> 00:01:43.765
It adds a disciplined investigative capability that helps the organization learn about

00:01:43.765 --> 00:01:48.020
its environment and respond to gaps before they become larger problems.
